    "reason": "evidence sufficient (proxy gate verdict; the open aspects need proposals): On its own, the cited item [ev-bd29b25491ac] is just a metric name. The section it comes from [ev-1f419676f177] explains what it means: metrics that started with `cortex_` now start with `loki_` because `metrics_namespace` defaults to `loki`. The same section says operators can keep the old prefix by setting `metrics_namespace` to `cortex`, and that this setting is deprecated. That gives enough to write the open aspects: subject is the metric `cortex_ruler_client_request_duration_seconds_sum`; change is a rename to `loki_ruler_client_request_duration_seconds_sum`; applicability is environments where `metrics_namespace` is not set to `cortex`; consequence is that anything querying the old metric name no longer finds it.",
